1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:06,243
This is Halden. Rivers bend, rails curve, and nothing lines up.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,440
So the map tells a useful lie. It throws away distance, and keeps the connections.

3
00:00:15,150 --> 00:00:20,000
Rule 1. Horizontal, vertical, or 45 degrees. Nothing else.

4
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:23,250
Rule 2. One line, one colour, one weight.

5
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:26,850
Rule 3. A tick is a stop. A ring is a change.

6
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:29,426
Zones tell you what it costs.

7
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:34,950
You are here, at Quill Lane. The lantern festival is at Rook Point.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,590
Fern line, change at Linden.

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,366
Round the Ring, change at Ember Wharf.

10
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:44,790
Saffron to the end.

11
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:50,100
A map doesn't show the city. It shows you the way.
